### Lessons

**Start here:** [Philosophy](00_philosophy.livemd): the moving line between human and machine code, the engineer as the bridge, and the 0 / 1 / N rule

**Part I: Ash foundations** (upstream, do these first)

0. to 9. [ash_tutorial](https://github.com/ash-project/ash_tutorial): Resources, Actions, Querying, Attributes, Customizing Actions, Relationships, Code Interfaces, Aggregates, Calculations

**Part II: LiveView with Ash** (before A2UI)

10. [LiveView: Reading Resources](10_liveview_reads.livemd): actors, `handle_params`, streams, no queries in `mount`
11. [LiveView: Forms & Actions](11_liveview_forms.livemd): `AshPhoenix.Form`, validation, errors from the action
12. [LiveView: Live Updates](12_liveview_pubsub.livemd): `Ash.Notifier.PubSub`, `connected?/1`
13. [Remote APIs as Resources](13_remote_resources.livemd): a REST API behind actions, generic and manual actions

**Part III: Working with your agent**

14. [Working With Your Agent](14_agent_tools.livemd): `ash_agent_tools`, Tidewave live eval, Serena over Expert, debugging "forbidden", the iron-law judge

**Part IV: The enterprise substrate**

15. [Events](15_events.livemd): `ash_events`, the event log as the record of *what happened*
16. [Projections](16_projections.livemd): `ash_events_projections`, grains, projectors, rebuilds
17. [Rules](17_rules.livemd): `ash_rules`, facts, absence semantics, the outcome lattice
18. [Compliance](18_compliance.livemd): `ash_compliance`, bundles, findings vs evaluations
19. [Decisions](19_decisions.livemd): `ash_decisions`, DMN and FEEL as versioned resources
20. [Approvals](20_approvals.livemd): `ash_bpmn` approval layer, maker-checker by subtraction
21. [Processes](21_process.livemd): `ash_bpmn` process layer, the three host seams
22. [Judgments](22_judgments.livemd): `ash_judgments`, models observe, declarations decide

**Part V: Experience and migration**

23. [A2UI](23_a2ui.livemd): `ash_a2ui`, UI surfaces derived from resources
24. [Strangler](24_strangler.livemd): `ash_strangler`, the new model over the legacy rows
25. [Capstone: The Ash Way](25_capstone.livemd): the whole refund flow, end to end

<!-- livebook:{"break_markdown":true} -->

### The story

Our support desk grows a **refund** workflow. A customer opens a ticket; a representative proposes a `Refund`. The refund is audited as events (15), counted per organization and day by a projection (16), checked against SLA and policy rules (17, 18), routed by a DMN decision (19), gated by an approval with maker-checker (20), orchestrated as a BPMN process when it gets complicated (21), triaged by a model that may *observe* but never *decide* (22), rendered as an agent-ready UI (23), and finally migrated off the old `helpdesk.cases` table that the 2011 app still writes to (24). Along the way you debug all of it with your agent the Ash way (14). The customer's billing record lives in a remote API, and it is a resource too (13).

